          "type": "text",
          "text": "# Task: userio multi-user OAuth rework + unified channel abstraction + ChatGPT-connectable MCP\n\nRepository: /home/roomhacker/agents-projects/universal-userio (Python, stdlib-first).\nWork ONLY in that repository. Tests: `python -m pytest tests/ -x -q` (or unittest if no\npytest). Do NOT commit — the lead commits/pushes.\n\nRead the code first: src/universal_userio/ (adapters.py, contracts.py, http_api.py,\nmcp_surface.py, mcp_transport.py, runtime.py, service.py, store.py). Current state:\nsingle-user service on loopback (127.0.0.1:18093), bearer-token /mcp, drafts/approval flow,\none shared account per channel (gmail-password extension, vk-inbox extension, telegram via\nQR service in universal-inbox sibling repo).\n\nOwner's requirements (verbatim intent):\n1. **Multi-user + OAuth**: many users; each user connects their OWN channels (their mail,\n   their telegram, their whatsapp). Add a user system: username/password login (seed the\n   owner account from env at first start — see below), issuing per-user tokens; the MCP\n   surface authenticates per user and scopes ALL data/operations to that user.\n2. **Owner seed**: on startup, if file `.env.owner-seed` exists (gitignored, format\n   KEY=VALUE with USERIO_SEED_USERNAME / USERIO_SEED_PASSWORD), create/update that user as\n   an owner. NEVER log or commit these values; the file already exists on the server.\n3. **Unified channel abstraction** — mail, telegram, whatsapp behind ONE interface:\n   - `list()` → chats/conversations (id, title/subject, last message snippet, unread);\n   - `read(chat_id | message_id)` → messages of a chat or one message (bounded text);\n   - `download(file_ref)` → file bytes/metadata;\n   - `send(chat_id, text, attachments?)` → goes through the EXISTING draft/approval flow\n     (do not bypass approvals; per-user outbound queue).\n   Rename/reshape MCP tools accordingly (userio.channels.list / read / download /\n   send_draft …) keeping backward-compatible aliases where cheap. Adapters that don't\n   support something return honest \"not supported by adapter\" instead of failing.\n4. **ChatGPT-connectable MCP**: expose an MCP endpoint usable as a ChatGPT custom\n   connector: public HTTPS path with per-user token auth (ChatGPT connectors pass a token\n   via OAuth or no-auth; pragmatic v1: support BOTH the existing JSON-RPC POST and SSE\n   (text/event-stream) streamable transport on /mcp, and document the connector setup\n   (URL + token). No new dependencies beyond stdlib.\n5. Keep the existing drafts/approvals/audit semantics and all current tests passing\n   (adapt tests where the API legitimately changes).\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Python stdlib only (http.server/sqlite3 as today). No frameworks.\n- Secrets only via env files (gitignored): .env (service) and .env.owner-seed (owner\n  login). Never print them.\n- Backward compatibility for exmanager's usage: bearer auth on /mcp with the existing\n  USERIO_API_TOKEN must KEEP WORKING as a \"service account\" that sees the owner user's\n  data (exmanager member_mcp uses http://127.0.0.1:18093/mcp with that token).\n- New users: created via owner-only MCP/HTTP endpoints (userio.users.create) with\n  username+password (hash passwords — PBKDF2 stdlib), per-user tokens (secrets) returned\n  once.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Multi-user store (users table, channels owned by user_id, per-user tokens).\n- OAuth-ish login: POST /auth/login {username,password} → {token}; token used as Bearer.\n- Unified channel tools per user; adapters refactored to the 4-method contract; existing\n  gmail/vk/telegram adapters wrapped.\n- SSE + JSON-RPC dual transport on /mcp; ChatGPT connector README section (RU).\n- Tests: multi-user isolation (user A cannot read user B chats), seed flow, unified\n  contract per adapter fake, SSE transport smoke, approval flow intact.\n\n## Report back\n\nChanged files + one-liners, test command + counts, how to create a user + connect ChatGPT,\nomissions.\n"
        }
      ],
